 "notes": "Source is a coach's typed results sheet that is two drafts pasted together: pages 1-3 use codes GR/FR, the later part (from Girls 100 m dash) uses G/F. Events printed twice were taken once, from the later corrected copy: Girls 100 m dash (later copy used; the earlier copy had Crowley 13.6, Kelley LR 15.9, Goodard FR 14.9, Moor GR 14.9 in place of Maine G 15.2, Edwards F 15.7, Keller LR 16.0 and Crowley 13.7), Boys 200 (later copy Wold 25.9; earlier 25.0), Boys/Girls 4x400 (earlier copy lumped boys and girls under 'Boys 4 x 400'; later copy split), and the earlier 'Boys 2 Mile' list (Price, Laughlin, Hunter, Carley, Little) which the later copy splits into Boys 3200 and Girls 3200. Places are the printed order within each list; several lists are not in mark order (e.g. Girls Discus Werneth 86-00 after Campbell 68-02, Boys Shot Stewart 27-00 after Kemna 24-04, Boys 400 Nason 1:42.0), and ties (12.8, 12.9, 13.9, 26.4) are numbered consecutively. Event names: the sheet's '2 Mile'/'3200' used as 3200 Meter Run; 'Racewalk' has no distance on the sheet, 1600 Meter Race Walk assumed. Boys 110 Hurdles and Girls 300 Hurdles are headers with no results. School codes: legend gives G/GR Greely, F/FR Freeport, OOB (not expanded by the legend; read as Old Orchard Beach, the only fit), LR Lake Region, Fa/FAL Falmouth (non-scoring); Fr read as Freeport. 'Mason - ?' and 'Oliver - ?' (Boys 100) have school '?' as printed. Moor (Girls 100) taken as Greely from the earlier copy's 'Moor - GR'. Dolat (Boys Discus, no code) taken as Greely, Dembowski (Boys Shot, no code) as Lake Region, from their coded rows elsewhere; Ewen in Girls 200 is coded G there. Falmouth non-scoring entries: Coyne, Keeler, Barbour. Names as printed incl. apparent typos (Camreon, Qugs, Themault->Therriault only in the later copy as printed there). Relay 'LR' and 'FR' codes expanded. Marks: 4x100 OOB 60.9 written 1:00.9; 400 m times printed in seconds (106.1, 113.8, 114.4, 116.6, 116.7, 102.0, 102.5) written as 1:46.1 etc.; later-copy times with dot separators (2.00.7, 9.57.9, 4.08.3, 14.30.0) written 2:00.7, 9:57.9, 4:08.3, 14:30.0. Field marks like 6' written 6-00. Unreadable-for-sure marks: Burgess GR Girls Discus '71'16\"' written 71-16 (16 inches impossible); Burg FR Girls Shot '23'20.25\"' written 23-20.25; Young GR Girls Shot '1'9.75\"' written 1-09.75 (likely 19-09.75 but not changed); Tomkinson LR Boys Discus printed '1070\"' read as 107-00 (a guess, not certain). Rows left out: (1) eleven unlabeled rows after Boys 800 on the last pages (Bosworth LR 15.0, Conchinski LR 16.6, Roy G 15.2, Small F 16.6, Smith OOB 16.1, Berg F 13.9, Wheeler G 17.6, Barry G 15.6, Benger G 17.0, Jordan G 18.6, Ewen 15.7), apparently the missing Boys 110 Hurdles but the sheet does not say so; (2) two orphan rows 'Flagg - LR - 59.7' and 'Koenigs - OOB - 106.5' after Boys Javelin, event unclear (400 m?); (3) five rows after a '++++' line in the later Girls 100 m dash (Curry F 15.00, Foster F 14.3, Monter F 18.4, Saffian G 15.3, O'Shea G 15.6), event unclear (hurdles?); (4) the earlier copy rows replaced as described above. No team scores are printed. Date from the title '@ Greely 5-14-09'. [review] 400 rows timed 1:5x (an 800 list pasted under the 400) and shot 1-09.75 left out."
